WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.285 --> 00:00:01.929
- (Bleep) you coffee.

00:00:01.929 --> 00:00:03.459
- It's not you, it's me.

00:00:03.459 --> 00:00:04.941
- Coffee, we've had some great times.

00:00:04.941 --> 00:00:06.709
But I just think we
need to see other people

00:00:06.709 --> 00:00:08.399
for a little while.

00:00:08.399 --> 00:00:10.752
(squeaking)

00:00:10.752 --> 00:00:12.956
(upbeat music)

00:00:12.956 --> 00:00:14.508
- So I drink a lot of coffee.

00:00:14.508 --> 00:00:17.403
- Every day, I drink about
two to three cups of coffee

00:00:17.403 --> 00:00:19.847
depending on my mood and my grogginess.

00:00:19.847 --> 00:00:21.979
- I think I just like having
a cup of coffee in my hand.

00:00:21.979 --> 00:00:23.580
I like having something to do.

00:00:23.580 --> 00:00:25.591
I don't like sitting at
my desk for too long,

00:00:25.591 --> 00:00:26.776
because it makes me go crazy.

00:00:26.776 --> 00:00:28.893
- For me to feel awake
throughout a work day,

00:00:28.893 --> 00:00:31.662
it used to be three or
four cups of coffee,

00:00:31.662 --> 00:00:33.814
and then it was five
or six cups of coffee,

00:00:33.814 --> 00:00:35.981
now it's six to eight cups of coffee.

00:00:35.981 --> 00:00:38.795
And with that increase of caffeine,

00:00:38.795 --> 00:00:42.135
I think I'm starting to develop anxiety.

00:00:42.135 --> 00:00:43.501
- I'm interested in cutting out coffee

00:00:43.501 --> 00:00:45.627
because I have anxiety and coffee

00:00:45.627 --> 00:00:47.301
definitely doesn't help that.

00:00:47.301 --> 00:00:49.274
- Taking a step back,
I'm thinking, you know,

00:00:49.274 --> 00:00:53.441
if you're really anxious,
maybe the cups of stimulants

00:00:55.404 --> 00:00:58.549
your pouring into your
mouth throughout the day

00:00:58.549 --> 00:01:00.716
is a thing to check in on.

00:01:02.369 --> 00:01:04.786
- Can caffeine cause anxiety?

00:01:05.705 --> 00:01:06.713
- Yes.

00:01:06.713 --> 00:01:10.162
So, caffeine can exacerbate
anxiety that already exists,

00:01:10.162 --> 00:01:14.843
but caffeine can also
independently cause anxiety.

00:01:14.843 --> 00:01:16.490
- That's kind of why I'm doing this.

00:01:16.490 --> 00:01:19.949
I'm trying to just quit cold turkey,

00:01:19.949 --> 00:01:21.761
and I'm not going to
have a drink of caffeine

00:01:21.761 --> 00:01:24.049
or anything else that has caffeine in it,

00:01:24.049 --> 00:01:28.216
for seven days, to see if I
can get this out of my system.

00:01:29.519 --> 00:01:31.259
- So, it's gonna be a
brutal first couple days.

00:01:31.259 --> 00:01:32.780
- Tomorrow is gonna be a nightmare.

00:01:32.780 --> 00:01:36.947
- What symptoms can we expect
by cutting out caffeine?

00:01:38.154 --> 00:01:40.301
- 50% of the time people
will experience a headache

00:01:40.301 --> 00:01:43.801
when they quit using caffeine cold turkey.

00:01:45.430 --> 00:01:48.673
Fatigue or sleepiness, you
know, just being more tired

00:01:48.673 --> 00:01:51.237
than usual, being very sleepy, yawning.

00:01:51.237 --> 00:01:52.879
Difficulty concentrating.

00:01:52.879 --> 00:01:54.811
Being depressed, irritable.

00:01:54.811 --> 00:01:57.207
And also, in certain
cases people experience

00:01:57.207 --> 00:01:59.417
a flu like syndrome.

00:01:59.417 --> 00:02:02.211
(bright music)

00:02:02.211 --> 00:02:05.378
- So as a replacement of coffee today,

00:02:06.533 --> 00:02:09.283
I figure I'm just gonna do water.

00:02:10.443 --> 00:02:14.031
Stay hydrated, I assume being
hydrated gives you energy.

00:02:14.031 --> 00:02:16.286
- I just woke up, it's day one,

00:02:16.286 --> 00:02:18.561
and I have so much to do today.

00:02:18.561 --> 00:02:21.904
I think today is gonna be a struggle.

00:02:21.904 --> 00:02:25.320
- So, day one without
coffee, and I'm already

00:02:25.320 --> 00:02:27.104
craving it real hard.

00:02:27.104 --> 00:02:31.253
So, I think I'm going to
get a giant bottle of water

00:02:31.253 --> 00:02:35.420
to hydrate, and hopefully that
will get rid of my craving.

00:02:38.081 --> 00:02:42.306
Day one was surprisingly not too intense.

00:02:42.306 --> 00:02:45.563
It felt like the calm
before the storm almost,

00:02:45.563 --> 00:02:49.618
because I've had caffeine
headaches and withdrawal before,

00:02:49.618 --> 00:02:52.185
but my first day not drinking coffee,

00:02:52.185 --> 00:02:54.155
I didn't have any headaches or anything,

00:02:54.155 --> 00:02:55.993
but I felt like something
was a little off.

00:02:55.993 --> 00:02:58.149
I don't know if it's
psychosomatic or what,

00:02:58.149 --> 00:03:00.649
but it's 3:30 and I feel like,

00:03:03.483 --> 00:03:06.756
I feel like I can just fall
asleep standing up right now.

00:03:06.756 --> 00:03:11.668
- My train was super delayed
and I'm already kinda grumpy,

00:03:11.668 --> 00:03:15.834
so I'm gonna try to find
something to hold me over,

00:03:15.834 --> 00:03:18.865
uncaffeinated, I don't know
how this is going to turn out.

00:03:18.865 --> 00:03:21.286
Day one I didn't do
anything to replace coffee,

00:03:21.286 --> 00:03:23.364
and I think that was my biggest problem.

00:03:23.364 --> 00:03:25.680
I just had a seltzer and
that do anything for me.

00:03:25.680 --> 00:03:26.796
The whole day was a haze,

00:03:26.796 --> 00:03:28.665
I felt like a zombie going through.

00:03:28.665 --> 00:03:30.995
- I would describe the first day,

00:03:30.995 --> 00:03:33.087
really as just tired.

00:03:33.087 --> 00:03:35.560
It's not quite coffee.

00:03:35.560 --> 00:03:37.579
I was just sleepy.

00:03:37.579 --> 00:03:40.534
I didn't feel any sort of
withdrawal from the coffee,

00:03:40.534 --> 00:03:43.417
I didn't feel sick, I don't
think I was irritable.

00:03:43.417 --> 00:03:45.632
This stuff does jack shit.

00:03:45.632 --> 00:03:47.008
That entire day at work,

00:03:47.008 --> 00:03:49.123
I really got very little accomplished

00:03:49.123 --> 00:03:52.457
because I couldn't stay
focused and I didn't feel like

00:03:52.457 --> 00:03:56.829
I was bringing anything
or any energy to my work.

00:03:56.829 --> 00:04:00.668
- So, the first day is over,
I'm walking out of work now.

00:04:00.668 --> 00:04:02.875
I did end up getting a
little bit of a headache,

00:04:02.875 --> 00:04:07.093
and I was like falling asleep standing up.

00:04:07.093 --> 00:04:10.884
- It's not even 8:30 and it
feels like it's midnight.

00:04:10.884 --> 00:04:15.138
The headache is, it's
spread to my whole forehead,

00:04:15.138 --> 00:04:17.665
it feels like somebody's just pushing in

00:04:17.665 --> 00:04:19.946
on the sides of my head constantly.

00:04:19.946 --> 00:04:23.779
- Caffeine is a drug
that directly antagonizes

00:04:25.534 --> 00:04:28.954
a certain receptor in the
brain called adenosine.

00:04:28.954 --> 00:04:30.856
And adenosine is a substance in the brain

00:04:30.856 --> 00:04:32.621
that sort of makes us sleepy.

00:04:32.621 --> 00:04:35.499
You're body is accustomed,
let's say, with seven or eight

00:04:35.499 --> 00:04:38.599
cups of coffee a day, to
having so much antagonism

00:04:38.599 --> 00:04:39.893
of adenosine.

00:04:39.893 --> 00:04:42.097
Then what happens is when
you abruptly remove it,

00:04:42.097 --> 00:04:44.426
now you have all this extra adenosine,

00:04:44.426 --> 00:04:46.294
because the body always compensates.

00:04:46.294 --> 00:04:47.726
So when you remove the caffeine,

00:04:47.726 --> 00:04:50.378
now you have more adenosine binding

00:04:50.378 --> 00:04:52.020
than you would be accustomed to,

00:04:52.020 --> 00:04:53.639
which makes you sleepy and tired,

00:04:53.639 --> 00:04:56.002
and it can also cause that throbbing,

00:04:56.002 --> 00:04:58.000
sensitive to movement headache.

00:04:58.000 --> 00:04:58.833
- [Man In Blue Shirt] There's a video

00:04:58.833 --> 00:05:00.544
that my girlfriend shot of me.

00:05:00.544 --> 00:05:03.043
I just passed out on the couch

00:05:03.043 --> 00:05:04.684
while we were watching television.

00:05:04.684 --> 00:05:06.348
And, in the video you see like,

00:05:06.348 --> 00:05:09.497
I am in the most uncomfortable position.

00:05:09.497 --> 00:05:12.645
And the next morning, I still
woke up and I was tired.

00:05:12.645 --> 00:05:16.497
- Usually caffeine withdrawal
peaks between about

00:05:16.497 --> 00:05:20.057
20 hours after your last
dose and about 60 hours

00:05:20.057 --> 00:05:21.412
after your last dose.

00:05:21.412 --> 00:05:24.892
So, sometime in the
first two to three days

00:05:24.892 --> 00:05:27.900
is when people will
experience the worst symptoms.

00:05:27.900 --> 00:05:30.268
(contemplative music)

00:05:30.268 --> 00:05:32.784
- The second day is when
I noticed the withdrawal.

00:05:32.784 --> 00:05:36.617
- Day two, walking to
work, and it is raining,

00:05:37.951 --> 00:05:40.034
and I have headaches now.

00:05:41.192 --> 00:05:43.863
Day two I started to actually
feel the physical symptoms,

00:05:43.863 --> 00:05:47.030
and that was probably the hardest day.

00:05:49.887 --> 00:05:53.234
- I had every intention
to go to the gym today,

00:05:53.234 --> 00:05:55.139
because I felt like that
would help me wake up.

00:05:55.139 --> 00:05:56.627
I still feel so tired.

00:05:56.627 --> 00:05:59.244
- I got my ass out of
bed at six A.M. somehow,

00:05:59.244 --> 00:06:02.411
and I'm headed in for a short workout.

00:06:03.820 --> 00:06:06.792
My energy got completely kick
started when I went to the gym

00:06:06.792 --> 00:06:09.259
and I felt really, really
good, better than if I had

00:06:09.259 --> 00:06:10.895
a cup of coffee in the morning.

00:06:10.895 --> 00:06:13.716
I'm hoping today goes a
lot better than yesterday.

00:06:13.716 --> 00:06:15.952
I'm feeling a little bit more
confident about the challenge,

00:06:15.952 --> 00:06:17.478
I think it's gonna get better.

00:06:17.478 --> 00:06:19.577
So think that was definitely
the key and I tried to

00:06:19.577 --> 00:06:22.163
stick with that throughout
the whole seven days,

00:06:22.163 --> 00:06:23.841
and I've noticed the days
that I do go to the gym

00:06:23.841 --> 00:06:25.788
I feel a lot better in the morning.

00:06:25.788 --> 00:06:29.064
- I also noticed how many
people on the subways

00:06:29.064 --> 00:06:30.955
or on the streets are holding coffee

00:06:30.955 --> 00:06:31.788
and how many coffee shops
there are in New York City.

00:06:31.788 --> 00:06:35.955
You can't walk a block with
passing three or four of them.

00:06:37.231 --> 00:06:40.592
(contemplative music)

00:06:40.592 --> 00:06:43.473
- The weekend became difficult.

00:06:43.473 --> 00:06:47.367
I went upstate to Tarrytown
with my girlfriend.

00:06:47.367 --> 00:06:50.407
We just wanted a nice
day outside the city,

00:06:50.407 --> 00:06:53.541
and so every corner
there are coffee shops.

00:06:53.541 --> 00:06:57.988
And the smell of coffee, just
like, wafting through the air.

00:06:57.988 --> 00:07:00.559
I knew that that was going
to become the worst day.

00:07:00.559 --> 00:07:02.245
I think this is a sign.

00:07:02.245 --> 00:07:04.601
And I felt bad for my girlfriend

00:07:04.601 --> 00:07:05.807
who was really enjoying that day,

00:07:05.807 --> 00:07:10.263
that I really wasn't present
because I was just so tired.

00:07:10.263 --> 00:07:12.513
So on day three, I cracked.

00:07:13.779 --> 00:07:17.696
On day three, I realized,
this is not something

00:07:19.236 --> 00:07:21.750
I'm able to do cold turkey.

00:07:21.750 --> 00:07:24.023
This is just one, this is just one.

00:07:24.023 --> 00:07:27.783
It's the weekend, I'm
very tired, just one.

00:07:27.783 --> 00:07:31.113
As soon as I tasted the
coffee on my tongue,

00:07:31.113 --> 00:07:33.679
my body started like,
getting ready for it.

00:07:33.679 --> 00:07:36.059
Like I already, the colors started getting

00:07:36.059 --> 00:07:37.164
